AltoERC4626RatioLinearDiscountOracle::constructor()
├── given invalid inputs
│   ├── when ERC4626 ratio node initialRatio is zero
│   │   └── it should revert with ModuleERC4626RatioInvalidInput
│   ├── when ERC4626 ratio node initialTimestamp is greater than block.timestamp
│   │   └── it should revert with ModuleERC4626RatioInvalidInput
│   ├── when ERC4626 ratio node maxYearlyGrowthRatioWad is zero
│   │   └── it should revert with ModuleERC4626RatioInvalidInput
│   ├── when linear discount node maturity is not in the future
│   │   └── it should revert with ModuleLinearDiscountInvalidInput
│   ├── when linear discount node ptToken is zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with ModuleLinearDiscountInvalidInput
│   ├── when linear discount node ptToken expiry does not match maturity
│   │   └── it should revert with ModuleLinearDiscountInvalidInput
│   ├── when linear discount node baseDiscountPerYear exceeds MATH_PRECISION
│   │   └── it should revert with ModuleLinearDiscountInvalidInput
│   ├── when linear discount node inDecimals + outDecimals exceeds 54
│   │   └── it should revert with ModuleLinearDiscountInvalidInput
│   └── when owner is zero address
│       └── it should revert with OwnableInvalidOwner
└── given valid inputs
    ├── it should set erc4626RatioNode correctly
    ├── it should set linearDiscountNode correctly
    ├── it should set owner correctly
    ├── it should emit SetERC4626RatioNode event
    └── it should emit SetLinearDiscountNode event
